cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LADAL in your research or teaching, please cite it using the metadata below. For individual tutorials, please use the citation provided on each tutorial page."

title: "LADAL — Language Technology and Data Analysis Laboratory"
abstract: "LADAL is a free, open-access research infrastructure providing tutorials, interactive tools, and structured courses for researchers, students, and educators working with language data. Established in 2019 at the University of Queensland, LADAL covers corpus linguistics, text analytics, statistics, data visualisation, and natural language processing, primarily using R. LADAL is part of the Language Data Commons of Australia (LDaCA), funded by the Australian Research Data Commons (ARDC) and the National Collaborative Research Infrastructure Strategy (NCRIS)."

